<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.1.4: Adding and Subtracting Polynomial Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01564</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.1.4: Adding and Subtracting Polynomial Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7787681a-e63d-4769-9f76-da2d430d987e</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity (15 minutes)</title>
<para>This activity pushes students’ mastery of adding and subtracting polynomials through the introduction of operations on polynomial functions.</para>
<para>As students solve the exercises, monitor for those who:</para>
<list>
  <item> are confused by the function notation when performing polynomial addition and subtraction skills learned in the previous activity in this lesson. </item>
  <item> do not distribute the subtraction sign through the entire function when subtracting a polynomial function. </item>
</list>
<title>Launch</title>
<para>Allow students to work through the problems individually. Have students work on the first 4 problems and pause the class for questions before students move on to subsequent questions.</para>
<title> Student Activity</title>
<para>Add the polynomial functions. Evaluate the sum for each given value.</para>
<para> \(z(x) = 8x^2 + 4x - 6\)          \(w(x) = -5x^2 + 2x + 3\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\( (z + w)(x) = \) ___________ </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((z + w)(x) = 3x^2 + 6x - 3\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\( (z + w)(6) = \) ___________ </item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((z + w)(6) = 141\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> \((z + w)(-9) = \) ___________ </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((z + w)(-9) = 186\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> \((z + w)(0)\) = ___________ </item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((z + w)(0) = -3\)</para>
<para>Subtract the polynomial functions. Evaluate the sum for each given value.</para>
<para>\(m(x) = -6x^2 + 2x - 8\)          \(n(x) = -x^2 - 7x - 6\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> \((m - n)(x) =\) ___________ </item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((m - n)(x) = -5x^2 + 9x - 2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> \((m - n)(-2) =\) ___________ </item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((m - n)(-2) = -40\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((m - n)(0) =\) ___________ </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((m - n)(0) = -2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item> \((m - n)(4) =\) ___________ </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((m - n)(4) = -46\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>What is a good way to check that you found the correct sum or difference when adding or subtracting polynomial functions? </item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Substitute a value for \(x\) into the individual polynomial functions. Add or subtract the results. The answer should be equal to the value you find when you substitute it into the sum or difference of the polynomial functions.</para>
<title>Video: Combining and Evaluating Polynomial Functions</title>
<para>Watch the following video to learn more about how to add and subtract polynomial functions and evaluate them at a given value:</para>
<div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-justify-content-center">
  <div class="os-raise-video-container"><video controls="true" crossorigin="anonymous">
      <source src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/eaecc03382b9de51eb04d6d681ab65c784d6e188">
      <track default="true" kind="captions" label="On" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/9ce97a7daeee9a7bec7f2554961f0695fb891989" srclang="en_us">https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/eaecc03382b9de51eb04d6d681ab65c784d6e188
    </track></source></video></div>
</div>


<title>Activity Synthesis</title>
<para>As discussed in the final question, emphasize that for any functions \(f(x)\) and \(g(x)\), \((f - g)(x) = f(x) - g(x)\). This can be a useful tool for evaluating that your solution to \((f - g)(x)\) is correct.</para>
<para>Ask students to verify this by finding \(z(6) + w(6)\) using the functions in the first part of the activity. The solution should match what they found for \((z + w)(6)\) in question 2.</para>
<title>6.1.4: Self Check</title>
<para><emphasis><emphasis>After the activity, students will answer the following question to check their understanding of the concepts explored in the activity</emphasis></emphasis>.</para>
<para><emphasis>QUESTION:</emphasis></para>
<para> For functions \(f(x)=5x^2-4x-1\) and \(g(x)=x^2+3x+8\), find:</para>
<para>\((f+g)(x) =\) _______</para>
<para>\((f+g)(5) =\) _______</para>
<table class="os-raise-textheavytable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        Answers
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        Feedback
      </entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>\((f+g)(x) = 4x^2-x+7\)</para>
        <para>\((f+g)(5) = 102\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>Incorrect. Let’s try again a different way: Check your operations when finding \((f+g)(x)\). The answer is \((f+g)(x) = 6x^2-x+7\) and \((f+g)(5) = 152\).</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>\((f+g)(x) = 6x^2-x+7\)</para>
        <para>\((f+g)(5) = 152\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>That’s correct! Check yourself: \((f+g)(x) = 5x^2-4x−1 + x^2+3x+8 = 6x^2-x+7\). Substitute 5 for \(x\) to find \((f+g)(5)\). \((f+g)(5) = 6(5)^2-(5)+7 = 150-5+7 = 152\).</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>\((f+g)(x) = 4x^2-7x-9\)</para>
        <para>\((f+g)(5) = 56\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>Incorrect. Let’s try again a different way: Did you find \((f-g)(x)\)? You need to find \((f+g)(x)\). The answer is \((f+g)(x) = 6x^2-x+7\) and \((f+g)(5) = 152\).</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>\((f+g)(x) = 6x^2-x+7\)</para>
        <para>\((f+g)(5) = 32\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>Incorrect. Let’s try again a different way: Did you square 5 in the first term when finding \((f+g)(5)\)? The answer is \((f+g)(x) = 6x^2-x+7\) and \((f+g)(5) = 152\).</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<title>6.1.4: Additional Resources</title>
<para><emphasis><emphasis>The following content is available to students who would like more support based on their experience with the self check. Students will not automatically have access to this content, so you may wish to share it with those who could benefit from it.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<title> Adding and Subtracting Polynomial Functions</title>
<para>Just as polynomials can be added and subtracted, polynomial functions can also be added and subtracted.</para>

<note>
  <para><emphasis>For functions \(f(x)\) and \(g(x)\),</emphasis></para>
  <hr/>
  <list>
    <item>\((f + g)(x) = f(x) + g(x)\)</item>
    <item>\((f - g)(x) = f(x) - g(x)\)</item>
  </list>
</note>

<para>Let’s look at some examples.</para>
<para>For the functions \(f(x) = 3x^2-5x+7\) and \(g(x) = x^2-4x-3\), find:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> \((f+g)(x)\) </item>
  <item>\(
    (f+g)(3)
    \)</item>
  <item>\(
    (f-g)(x)
    \)</item>
  <item>\(
    (f-g)(-2)
    \)</item>
</list>
<para>The following is a step-by-step breakdown.
</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((f+g)(x)=f(x)+g(x)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 - 
  </emphasis>Substitute </para>
<para>\(f(x)={\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}{\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}{\style{color:red}+}{\style{color:red}7}\) and \(g(x)={\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}{\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}{\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}3}\).
  \((f+g)(x)=({\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}{\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}{\style{color:red}+}{\style{color:red}7})+{\style{color:blue}(}{\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}{\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}{\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}3}{\style{color:blue})}\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 - 
  </emphasis>Rewrite without the parentheses.</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(x)=3x^2-5x+7-x^2-4x-3\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 - 
  </emphasis>Put like terms together.</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(x)=3x^2+x^2-5x-4x+7-3\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> Combine like terms.</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(x)=4x^2-9x+4\)</para>
<para>In part (a), we found \((f+g)(x)\), and now are asked to find \((f+g)(3)\).</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((f+g)(x)=4x^2-9x+4\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 - 
  </emphasis>To find \((f+g)(3)\), substitute \(x=3\).</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(3)=4(3)^2-9 \cdot 3+4\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Simplify. </para>
<para>  \((f+g)(3)=4 \cdot 9-9 \cdot 3+ 4\)
  \((f+g)(3)=36-27+4\)
  \((f+g)(3)=13\)</para>
<para>Notice that we could have found \((f+g)(3)\) by first finding the values of \(f(3)\) and \(g(3)\) separately and then adding the results.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> Find \(f (3)\).</para>
<para>  \(f(x)=3x^2-5x+7\)
  \( f({\style{color:red}3})=3({\style{color:red}3})^2-5({\style{color:red}3})+7\)
  \(f(3)=19\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Find \(g(3)\).</para>
<para>  \(g(x)=x^2-4x-3\)
  \(g(3)=-6\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 - 
  </emphasis>Find \((f+g)(3)\).</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(x)=f(x)+g(x)\)
  \((f+g)(3)=f(3)+g(3)\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> Substitute \(f(3)={\style{color:red}1}{\style{color:red}9}\) and \(g(3)= {\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}6}\).</para>
<para>  \((f+g)(3)=19+(-6)\)
  \((f+g)(3)=13\)</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((f-g)(x)=f(x)-g(x)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 - 
  </emphasis>Substitute </para>
<para>\(f(x)={\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}{\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}{\style{color:red}+}{\style{color:red}7}\) and \(g(x)= {\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}{\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}{\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}3}\).
  \((f-g)(x)=( {\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}{\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}{\style{color:red}+}{\style{color:red}7})-({\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}{\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}{\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}3})\) </para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 - 
  </emphasis>Rewrite without the parentheses.</para>
<para>  \((f-g)(x)=3x^2-5x+7-x^2+4x+3\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Put like terms together.</para>
<para>  \((f-g)(x)=3x^2-x^2-5x+4x+7+3\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> Combine like terms.</para>
<para>  \((f-g)(x)=2x^2-x+10\)</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((f-g)(x)=2x^2-x+10\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> To find \((f-g)(-2)\), substitute \(x={\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2}\).</para>
<para>  \((f-g)( {\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2})=2({\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2})^2-({\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2})+10\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Simplify.</para>
<para>  \((f-g)(-2)=2 \cdot 5-(-2)+10\)
  \((f-g)(-2)=20\)</para>

<title> Try It: Adding and Subtracting Polynomial Functions</title>
<para>For functions \(f(x)=2x^2-4x+3\) and \(g(x)=x^2-2x-6\), find:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((f+g)(x)\)</item>
  <item>\((f+g)(3)\)</item>
  <item>\((f-g)(x)\)</item>
  <item>\((f-g)(-2)\)</item>
</list>
<para>Write down your answers. Then select the<emphasis> Solution </emphasis>button to compare your work.</para>
<title> Solution</title>
<para>Here is how to add and subtract the polynomial functions:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(\begin{array}{rcl}(f+g)(x)&amp;=&amp;(2x^2-4x+3)+(x^2-2x-6)\\&amp;=&amp;2x^2-4x+3+x^2-2x-6\\&amp;=&amp;3x^2-6x-3\end{array}\)
  </item>
  <item> \(\begin{array}{rcl}(f+g)(3)&amp;=&amp;3(3)^2-6(3)-3\\&amp;=&amp;3(9)-6(3)-3\\&amp;=&amp;27-18-3\\&amp;=&amp;6\end{array}\)
  </item>
  <item>\(\begin{array}{rcl}(f-g)(x)&amp;=&amp;(2x^2-4x+3)-(x^2-2x-6)\\&amp;=&amp;2x^2-4x+3-x^2+2x+6\\&amp;=&amp;x^2-2x+9\;\end{array}\)
  </item>
  <item>\(\begin{array}{rcl}(f-g)(-2)&amp;=&amp;(-2)^2-2(-2)+9\;\\&amp;=&amp;(4)+4+9\;\\&amp;=&amp;17\;\end{array}\)</item>
</list></section>
</content>
